    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>it's just hard to see it that way. when the spark is gone, it's not just a phase or a rut. it's like the light has actually gone out. i look at a blank canvas and i don't see potential, i just see a void. it's exhausting pretending that there's something more coming when you can feel that you've reached the natural conclusion of your purpose. isn't there a certain peace in just accepting that the well is dry?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
